From 207e6cf60ce7c0092e5ffbf296166b7863b25770 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Feb 2024 17:13:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: stm32/hash - fix negative size in DMA scatterwalk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is an issue in stm32_hash_prepare_request(). While building the
aligned sglist used by the DMA engine, a negative size can be passed to
scatterwalk_map_and_copy(), which in turn results in an invalid pointer
being computed.

The problem is caused by an optimization in stm32_hash_prepare_request()
that tries to speed up alignment of the input data. This optimization is
not compatible with the omap_sham_copy_sgs() implementation and can lead
to the negative size being computed.

Dropping this unnecessary optimization fixes the issue.

Change-Id: Ie0c58c08909c1e5f02753916a3f663cb98cd4a93
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c | 11 -----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c
@@ -1288,17 +1288,6 @@ static int stm32_hash_prepare_request(st
 
 	rctx->total = nbytes;
 
-	if (update && req->nbytes && (!IS_ALIGNED(state->bufcnt, bs))) {
-		int len = bs - state->bufcnt % bs;
-
-		if (len > req->nbytes)
-			len = req->nbytes;
-		scatterwalk_map_and_copy(state->buffer + state->bufcnt, req->src,
-					 0, len, 0);
-		state->bufcnt += len;
-		rctx->offset = len;
-	}
-
 	/* copy buffer in a temporary one that is used for sg alignment */
 	if (state->bufcnt)
 		memcpy(hdev->xmit_buf, state->buffer, state->bufcnt);
